## User preferences

- when the user said "Hey, messages are going out. I need to replenish my Sendelio balance. Could you stop the campaigns?" -> treat this as a stop-the-line production request and verify the live send surface before acting [Task 1]
- when the user asked "What about the messages that were sent that had errors there?" -> separate queued, failed, sent, and delivered rows instead of mixing them into one campaign status answer [Task 2]
- when the user said "I just want to make sure we can re-key those messages once I increase the balance" -> default to a safe retry plan that preserves content, respects opt-outs/suppression, and re-spaces sends from now instead of blindly replaying old scheduled rows [Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- In Sandra, the decisive emergency stop point is the outbound `messages` rows still at `status='queued'`; a campaign can look completed while queued rows remain because the drain path keys off `messages.scheduled_for <= now()` [Task 1]
- Release logic refuses any row whose status is no longer `queued`, so flipping queued Sendillo/Sendelio rows to a terminal non-sendable state is an effective production brake without deleting history [Task 1]
- The stop action that worked here was: snapshot the live state locally, mark queued outbound `provider='sendillo'` rows as failed with `failed_at` plus a stop reason, then archive unarchived SMS campaigns with `archived_at` set [Task 1]
- The local rollback/audit snapshot for this run was `/tmp/sandra-campaign-stop-rollback-2026-06-26T13-54-55-904Z.json` [Task 1]
- The retry-safe set from this incident was the intentionally stopped 2,045 queued rows plus 1,513 balance/capability failures that had no provider external ID; opt-out and suppression failures remain terminal exclusions [Task 2]
- `06.23.26-Condos-SMS-DealMachine` carried the balance/capability failures in this run, while `6.22.26-Tired-Landlords` only showed opt-out/suppression failures [Task 2]
- No `sent` or `delivered` rows carried the balance/capability error string in this rollout, so the "errors" the user asked about were failed attempts rather than post-send failures [Task 2]

## Failures and how to do differently

- symptom: a campaign appears completed but messages are still going out; cause: queued outbound rows still exist in `messages` and the cron drain releases anything still queued and due; fix: inspect and neutralize the queued `messages` rows, not just campaign status [Task 1]
- symptom: the checked-in repo does not make the campaign table shape obvious enough for a safe live write; cause: schema truth is incomplete in migrations or local assumptions; fix: inspect production schema directly before issuing the stop write [Task 1]
- symptom: a retry plan risks blasting old rows immediately after balance top-up; cause: old `scheduled_for` values are left in place when rows are re-queued; fix: re-space retryable rows from "now" using campaign pacing rules [Task 2]
- symptom: all failed rows get marked retryable; cause: balance failures are not separated from opt-out or suppression failures; fix: split retry-safe balance/stop rows from terminal exclusions before any requeue plan [Task 2]

